{
  "_comment": [
    "Offline map packages Roadguard can install.",
    "",
    "These are PMTiles archives of the Protomaps Basemap build of OpenStreetMap data, published as",
    "release assets of github.com/tunlezah/DashCam and downloaded once, on first run. After that the",
    "map renders entirely from the local file: no tile server, no glyph server, no sprite server.",
    "",
    "Whole-of-Australia is the default so that a driver crossing a state border never loses the map.",
    "It stops at zoom 12, which shows the highway and main-road network but not every suburban",
    "street. A single-state package goes to zoom 14, which is street level, and is the better choice",
    "for anyone who mostly drives in one state -- the app says so where the choice is offered.",
    "",
    "sizeBytes and maxZoom were read from the published artifacts themselves (HTTP content-length,",
    "and the PMTiles v3 header), not from a build log. sha256 is deliberately empty: the assets can",
    "be republished by their own workflow, and a stale pinned hash would make Roadguard reject a",
    "perfectly good archive. Integrity is instead checked structurally -- PMTiles magic, version,",
    "tile type, zoom range, published size, and the presence of every vector layer the bundled style",
    "draws -- which also catches the failure a checksum cannot: a valid archive in the wrong schema.",
    "See docs/offline-maps.md."
  ],
